.TH WADB 1 "2026-08-15" "wadb" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wadb \- pair Android devices over ADB Wi\-Fi via a terminal QR code
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wadb
.RI [ flags ]
.br
.B wadb
.RI [ flags ]
.B connect
.br
.B wadb
.RI [ flags ]
.B doctor
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wadb
prints a QR code in the terminal. Scanning it from
.B Settings \(-> Developer options \(-> Wireless debugging \(-> Pair device with QR code
on an Android 11+ device pairs the device with this host and connects it over
ADB Wi\-Fi, then
.B wadb
exits.
.PP
This is the same protocol Android Studio uses for
.IR "Pair device using Wi-Fi" .
The phone and the host must share a Wi\-Fi network with no AP isolation, and
Wireless debugging must be enabled in Developer options.
.PP
.B wadb
generates a single\-use service name and password, renders them as a QR code,
waits for the device to announce
.B _adb\-tls\-pairing._tcp
over mDNS, and runs
.BR "adb pair" .
It then waits for the
.B _adb\-tls\-connect._tcp
announce and runs
.BR "adb connect" .
The TLS pairing handshake itself is handled by
.BR adb (1).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B connect
Reconnect a device that is already paired with this host, without printing a QR
code. Pairing survives reboots and Wi\-Fi changes, but the port Android listens
on does not, so this is the command to reach for when a known device stops
appearing in
.BR "adb devices" .
.TP
.B doctor
Report the local
.BR adb ,
its platform\-tools version, the network interfaces worth passing to
.BR \-\-iface ,
and the mDNS services
.B adb
can see.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-adb " path"
Path to the adb binary. By default
.B wadb
looks in $ANDROID_HOME, $ANDROID_SDK_ROOT, the standard Android Studio SDK
locations, $PATH, and the Homebrew commandline\-tools directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-iface " name"
Browse for mDNS on a single network interface instead of all of them. Use this
when a VPN tunnel, a container bridge, or a second NIC swallows the multicast
traffic. An unusable name is rejected immediately.
.TP
.B \-\-pair\-only
Pair the device, then exit without running
.BR "adb connect" .
Useful when pairing succeeds but the device delays or hides its connect
announce.
.TP
.B \-\-qr\-ascii
Render the QR code with plain ASCII blocks, for fonts and emulators that render
half blocks poorly.
.TP
.B \-\-qr\-invert
Invert the QR code, for terminals with a light background.
.TP
.B \-\-qr\-sixel
Render the QR code as a sixel image. Requires a terminal that implements the
sixel protocol, and scans under any color theme.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Print discovered mDNS service entries to standard error.
.TP
.BI \-\-pair\-timeout " duration"
How long to wait for the pairing announce. Default 2m.
.TP
.BI \-\-connect\-timeout " duration"
How long to wait for the connect announce. Default 30s.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.B \-v
is a shorthand.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Every option above has an environment equivalent; command\-line flags override
it.
.TP
.B WADB_ADB
Same as
.BR \-\-adb .
.TP
.B WADB_IFACE
Same as
.BR \-\-iface .
.TP
.B WADB_PAIR_ONLY
Same as
.BR \-\-pair\-only .
.TP
.B WADB_QR_ASCII
Same as
.BR \-\-qr\-ascii .
.TP
.B WADB_QR_INVERT
Same as
.BR \-\-qr\-invert .
.TP
.B WADB_QR_SIXEL
Same as
.BR \-\-qr\-sixel .
.TP
.B WADB_VERBOSE
Same as
.BR \-\-verbose .
.TP
.B WADB_PAIR_TIMEOUT
Same as
.BR \-\-pair\-timeout .
.TP
.B WADB_CONNECT_TIMEOUT
Same as
.BR \-\-connect\-timeout .
.PP
Boolean variables accept values such as true, false, 1, or 0. Duration
variables accept values such as 30s or 3m.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Paired and connected, or the requested command completed.
.TP
.B 1
Pairing, discovery, or connecting failed.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments or environment values.
.SH EXAMPLES
Pair and connect a new device:
.PP
.RS
.EX
wadb
.EE
.RE
.PP
Reconnect a device paired earlier, over a specific interface:
.PP
.RS
.EX
wadb \-\-iface en0 connect
.EE
.RE
.PP
Diagnose a discovery problem:
.PP
.RS
.EX
wadb doctor
wadb \-\-verbose
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR adb (1)
.PP
Project home: https://github.com/LinDevHard/wadb
